  "_about": "BRONTOTHERIUM / MEGACEROPS (Eocene-Oligocene North America, 2026-11-08; generator tools/creaturegen/prehistoric/gen.py): a brontothere bull about 5 m long and 2.5 m at the withers -- rhino- and elephant-like, a high HUMP over the shoulders (the thoracic spines) and the back sloping down to a lower rump, a deep barrel on thick pillar legs, four hoof-nails on the fore feet and three on the hind; a long head with a concave, SADDLE-SHAPED profile (the back of the skull high, the face dipping, the nose rising again), wide cheekbones, small eyes, and at the end of the nose the forked BONY HORN -- a Y: one broad shared stem, two skin-covered prongs flattened fore-and-aft diverging up, out and a little forward to blunt squarish ends; a short tail with a dark brush; grey-brown hide. Horns and nails sharp `horn`s faired into the skin, the ears the rhinoceros' cupped `fin` scaled. Coats grey-brown, brown, grey; variant `cow` (smaller, short horns)."
